# Secrets. `.env.*` is ignored so real credential files can never be committed,
# but the tracked `*.example` templates must stay committable — otherwise the
# ignore rule silently swallows the documentation for every service.
# NOTE: the glob must be `*.env*.example`, NOT `*.env.example`. Git's `*`
# does not cross `/`, and `.env.prod.example` ends in `.prod.example` — so
# `!**/*.env.example` would NOT re-include it and the template would vanish.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env*.example
# Real per-service production env files (compose env_file targets).
.env.prod
**/.env.prod
# Captured Pocket Option browser session. Only the CREDENTIAL artifacts are
# ignored — NOT the whole `session/` directory, which also holds tracked
# maintenance scripts (capture_session.py, refresh_ssid.py). A broad
# `session/` rule would silently block new scripts from being committed.
pocket-bridge/session/*.json
pocket-bridge/session/*cookie*
pocket-bridge/session/*.txt
pocket-bridge/session/__pycache__/

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
coverage/
**/coverage/
# TypeScript incremental-build cache. Machine-specific and regenerated by every
# `tsc --build`; committing it makes `git status` permanently dirty and can
# ship a STALE cache into an image, where it would let tsc skip a recheck.
*.tsbuildinfo

.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
**/venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

*.log
*.log.*
*_log.txt
*_err.txt
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*-check.png
# Ad-hoc verification artifacts: before/after UI screenshots kept at the repo
# root during a change, and one-off websocket probe scripts. These are local
# evidence of a single investigation, not source — leaving them untracked
# risks sweeping them into an unrelated commit.
p*-grid-*.png
**/p*_ws_probe.mjs
*.tmp
*.temp
*.zip
*_exit.txt

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

*.local
*.local.*
